00:02:03.331 --> 00:02:05.700
- [Voiceover] June asks, "My
husband is a big picture

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.312
"kind of guy, but so is his wishlist.

00:02:08.312 --> 00:02:11.558
"Any advice on Christmas
shopping for this type?"

00:02:11.558 --> 00:02:14.297
- June, this is a great question.

00:02:14.297 --> 00:02:16.492
If he's a big picture kinda guy like I am,

00:02:16.492 --> 00:02:19.169
I can answer this
perfectly so I hope he is

00:02:19.169 --> 00:02:21.580
because I know exactly what I want,

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.373
which is one-of-a-kind experiences

00:02:25.373 --> 00:02:28.460
or effort, let me explain, meaning,

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.010
you don't need to spend a lotta money.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.134
For example, here is the greatest gift

00:02:32.134 --> 00:02:33.579
that Lizzie could ever get me.

00:02:33.579 --> 00:02:35.495
She could go around for months,

00:02:35.495 --> 00:02:37.236
my 40th is coming up next November,

00:02:37.236 --> 00:02:40.110
she can go around and
interview every person

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.582
that I've ever met, or she should come

00:02:42.582 --> 00:02:44.585
to Vayner and basically get everybody

00:02:44.585 --> 00:02:48.242
on video telling me that
I'm the greatest, right?

00:02:48.242 --> 00:02:51.304
That to me is an ultimate present

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:54.180
and it's unscalable, that's a lotta work.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.688
To me, the way to really wow your husband

00:02:56.688 --> 00:03:00.068
is to make something
that is a one-of-a-kind

00:03:00.068 --> 00:03:02.799
and something that is not scalable.

00:03:02.799 --> 00:03:04.541
See, my friends, the reason people

00:03:04.541 --> 00:03:07.457
like those kind of gifts is it's effort.

00:03:07.457 --> 00:03:09.143
Money...

00:03:10.063 --> 00:03:12.360
A lot of times, listen,
it's hard to get money,

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.226
but a lot of money from a
gifting standpoint is easy.

00:03:16.226 --> 00:03:18.037
You spend and you buy
something, that's great.

00:03:18.037 --> 00:03:22.165
But your time, your effort,
your heart and soul,

00:03:22.165 --> 00:03:23.575
those are the things you can't replace,

00:03:23.575 --> 00:03:26.674
and so for my wife and I
and the likeminded people

00:03:26.674 --> 00:03:29.130
that I've met in my life, it
is about those experiences.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.654
It's about the dinner that you have

00:03:31.654 --> 00:03:33.623
that's special that somebody cooks,

00:03:33.623 --> 00:03:35.973
or when somebody makes something.

00:03:35.973 --> 00:03:39.182
Lizzie got me a gift for
our 10th wedding anniversary

00:03:39.182 --> 00:03:41.684
that I'll keep to myself
that is so incredible

00:03:41.684 --> 00:03:44.363
and it speaks to that
world, and so I would try

00:03:44.363 --> 00:03:46.405
to do something that's not scalable.

00:03:46.405 --> 00:03:50.131
Call up five of his
best friends growing up

00:03:50.131 --> 00:03:51.907
that he's fallen out of touch with

00:03:51.907 --> 00:03:54.032
and have them create an audio podcast

00:03:54.032 --> 00:03:56.871
of reminiscing of stories
when they were kids,

00:03:56.871 --> 00:03:58.891
something that just isn't replicatable,

00:03:58.891 --> 00:04:00.544
something that can't be bought,

00:04:00.544 --> 00:04:04.512
something that took your
effort to execute for him.

00:04:05.252 --> 00:04:09.251
- [Voiceover] Antoine asks,
"What keeps you up at night?"

00:04:09.251 --> 00:04:11.396
- Antoine, that's a very
quick and easy question,

00:04:11.396 --> 00:04:14.042
literally, and I think
at some level the reason

00:04:14.042 --> 00:04:15.637
I took this question 'cause it's not--

00:04:15.637 --> 00:04:17.503
I've probably even addressed
this before with VaynerNation,

00:04:17.503 --> 00:04:20.970
but every so often it's a worthwhile

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:25.385
venture to bring it up again, which is

00:04:26.495 --> 00:04:28.502
the only thing that keeps me up at night

00:04:28.502 --> 00:04:30.961
is the things that I can't control

00:04:30.961 --> 00:04:32.637
and the only thing that I can't control

00:04:32.637 --> 00:04:36.541
that really cripples me is
the health of my family.

00:04:36.541 --> 00:04:39.813
The health of my family is
what keeps me up at night,

00:04:39.813 --> 00:04:41.903
which is just something I can't control.

00:04:41.903 --> 00:04:45.508
I can do everything right, but an accident

00:04:45.508 --> 00:04:47.649
or something unfortunate or a disease

00:04:47.649 --> 00:04:50.798
that we all hate so much can come along

00:04:50.798 --> 00:04:52.855
and change the course of my life.

00:04:52.855 --> 00:04:54.685
When it comes to business, when it comes

00:04:54.685 --> 00:04:57.778
to my relationships, I
feel in utter control

00:04:57.778 --> 00:05:02.744
and I really, really recommend
to a lot of people here...

00:05:03.794 --> 00:05:06.752
It's amazing to me in
the stress-filled world

00:05:06.752 --> 00:05:10.268
that I live in, by outside
standards, my calendar,

00:05:10.268 --> 00:05:13.100
what I'm trying to achieve,
my own stress on that,

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.660
all the things that are pulling at me,

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.397
none of it stresses me because

00:05:19.397 --> 00:05:20.627
it's gonna be what it's gonna be.

00:05:20.627 --> 00:05:22.791
I'm gonna execute
against my skill and some

00:05:22.791 --> 00:05:25.038
of the serendipity that
comes along with the game

00:05:25.038 --> 00:05:27.232
and I'm very comfortable
and zen in that game.

00:05:27.232 --> 00:05:29.269
But the thing that does bother me,

00:05:29.269 --> 00:05:31.575
the thing that makes me
upset or I'm concerned about

00:05:31.575 --> 00:05:35.116
is 100 percent the
well-being of my family.

00:05:35.116 --> 00:05:38.864
- Gary Vaynerchuk, I have
an #AskGaryVee question.

00:05:38.864 --> 00:05:41.140
I'm here in Tasmania at the opening

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:46.120
of a brand-new cellar door
winery and oyster bar.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.654
It's a small three hectare
vineyard, seven acres.

00:05:48.654 --> 00:05:51.088
Now, I'm gonna ask you a question.

00:05:51.088 --> 00:05:56.010
If you had a seven acre
vineyard and it didn't

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:59.034
have these wonderful
views that we have here,

00:05:59.034 --> 00:06:02.141
how would you sell lots of wine?

00:06:02.141 --> 00:06:03.759
How would you do things different

00:06:03.759 --> 00:06:06.390
to all the other vineyards
that are out there?

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:08.890
Cheers, I love you, boy, thank you.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.903
- Ah, it's nice to see the wine stuff

00:06:11.903 --> 00:06:13.721
show up in the #AskGaryVee Show.

00:06:13.721 --> 00:06:15.148
I really appreciate the question.

00:06:15.148 --> 00:06:17.981
First off all, I've been to
Tasmania, an incredible place,

00:06:17.981 --> 00:06:19.292
making some of the most interesting

00:06:19.292 --> 00:06:21.729
sparkling and Pinot noir-based wines

00:06:21.729 --> 00:06:23.769
that I think are coming out of the world,

00:06:23.769 --> 00:06:26.801
yet so many Americans don't
know it and it's really sad.

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:28.577
Think about how many of
you when you hear Tasmania

00:06:28.577 --> 00:06:31.485
thought about the Tasmanian
Devil cartoon character

00:06:31.485 --> 00:06:34.011
and that's all you got,
which is really too bad

00:06:34.011 --> 00:06:36.461
considering how incredible the place is.

00:06:36.461 --> 00:06:39.423
Look, I think that we've addressed my--

00:06:39.423 --> 00:06:41.168
You know, it's funny, we made a movie.

00:06:41.168 --> 00:06:43.082
DRock, you crushed it,
let's link it right here

00:06:43.082 --> 00:06:45.148
'cause I know you can do
that in the YouTube world.

00:06:45.148 --> 00:06:47.694
The Clouds and the Dirt, and
the answer to your question

00:06:47.694 --> 00:06:50.324
are really clouds and dirt,
or as, way is that I used

00:06:50.324 --> 00:06:53.284
to say it to my dad, big and small.

00:06:53.284 --> 00:06:56.238
The way I would sell a lot of
wine is we'd be big and small.

00:06:56.238 --> 00:06:58.674
Let me explain, you've got
a small kind of parcel,

00:06:58.674 --> 00:07:00.157
you're not making that much wine,

00:07:00.157 --> 00:07:03.093
and so the small would be handselling.

00:07:03.093 --> 00:07:05.521
I'd be flying over to Australia,

00:07:05.521 --> 00:07:08.727
I would be going into the big
cities within New Zealand,

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:10.943
I would probably pick one
or two markets in Asia,

00:07:10.943 --> 00:07:13.252
and I would literally fly in and hustle.

00:07:13.252 --> 00:07:16.858
Literally knock on doors,
walk around with sommeliers

00:07:16.858 --> 00:07:19.731
and salespeople from the companies
that represented my wine,

00:07:19.731 --> 00:07:21.907
and one by one, restaurant by restaurant,

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:24.153
retailer by retailer, sell the product.

00:07:24.153 --> 00:07:25.686
Taste and sell, taste and sell.

00:07:25.686 --> 00:07:27.864
The unscalable, the small.

00:07:27.864 --> 00:07:30.005
Now on the big, and you've
heard me give this advice

00:07:30.005 --> 00:07:32.583
in the past, I would
become a media company.

00:07:32.583 --> 00:07:34.707
Now look, it's very easy for me to say

00:07:34.707 --> 00:07:37.041
that that's what I would do
because I actually did it.

00:07:37.041 --> 00:07:39.931
In 2006, while doing the small stuff,

00:07:39.931 --> 00:07:41.882
the tactical e-mail service, the website,

00:07:41.882 --> 00:07:43.466
building a wine shop, working the

00:07:43.466 --> 00:07:45.208
floor on a Saturday and selling.

00:07:45.208 --> 00:07:46.764
If you haven't seen my comeback video,

00:07:46.764 --> 00:07:47.404
(snaps fingers)

00:07:47.404 --> 00:07:49.636
I know, a lot of editing, Staphon.

00:07:51.576 --> 00:07:53.259
Those are the small things, but the big

00:07:53.259 --> 00:07:55.584
things were Wine Library TV, right?

00:07:55.584 --> 00:07:57.719
I decided to make myself The Critic.

00:07:57.719 --> 00:08:00.742
I would if I were you for your winery

00:08:00.742 --> 00:08:04.017
become the authority of food and wine,

00:08:04.017 --> 00:08:05.591
food and wine, I wouldn't
go lifestyle and travel,

00:08:05.591 --> 00:08:08.102
but I would be the
authority of food and wine

00:08:08.102 --> 00:08:12.243
for New Zealand food and wine,
the cuisine and the wines.

00:08:12.243 --> 00:08:16.377
I would actually review and
talk about your competitors.

00:08:16.377 --> 00:08:19.314
With a small parcel, you're
not competing with anybody,

00:08:19.314 --> 00:08:22.344
really, 'cause there's room
for everybody at that level.

00:08:22.344 --> 00:08:24.696
So I would literally turn yourself,

00:08:24.696 --> 00:08:26.052
and clearly you're a very charismatic

00:08:26.052 --> 00:08:28.651
and good-looking man on
video, you just did it.

00:08:28.651 --> 00:08:29.919
You felt comfortable doing it.

00:08:29.919 --> 00:08:31.781
I would execute that at scale.

00:08:31.781 --> 00:08:35.248
Literally replicate what I
did by putting out content,

00:08:35.248 --> 00:08:36.873
whether video, which I think you should do

00:08:36.873 --> 00:08:39.125
based on what I saw, or written form.

00:08:39.125 --> 00:08:41.586
Become an authority, you
need to be a media company.

00:08:41.586 --> 00:08:43.380
You need to be bigger than you are brought

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:46.236
to you by your wine, so
I would go big and small.

00:08:46.236 --> 00:08:48.768
But by the way, don't get
caught up in the glam.

00:08:48.768 --> 00:08:51.007
While I was showing up on Conan

00:08:51.007 --> 00:08:53.132
and everybody was quoting me for TV shows

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:56.318
and everything was great, I
was still downstairs hustling,

00:08:56.318 --> 00:08:58.059
trying to sell one more
bottle of Pinot noir.

00:08:58.059 --> 00:09:00.009
I was still in my office to 11 PM

00:09:00.009 --> 00:09:02.222
answering people on Twitter,
answering my e-mails

00:09:02.222 --> 00:09:04.137
tryin' to get a good deal on a Barolo.

00:09:04.137 --> 00:09:06.119
I was still doing the small.

00:09:06.119 --> 00:09:08.613
It's not playing in the
middle, it's going big.

00:09:08.613 --> 00:09:11.643
You need to become the authority

00:09:11.643 --> 00:09:14.011
of New Zealand food and
wine, and the small,

00:09:14.011 --> 00:09:15.665
and you have to have the humility

00:09:15.665 --> 00:09:18.243
to get on a plane, sit in
the middle aisle and go

00:09:18.243 --> 00:09:20.742
to the Philippines, and
sell a couple of bottles

00:09:20.742 --> 00:09:24.253
to some random restaurant, got it?

00:09:25.213 --> 00:09:27.490
- [Voiceover] Scout asks,
"Should all young companies

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:30.067
"have a sleeper website as a strategy

00:09:30.067 --> 00:09:31.860
"to not let the competition know how big

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:35.134
"you're getting or will
it hurt the brand?"

00:09:35.134 --> 00:09:37.137
- Scout, I assume you're asking this

00:09:37.137 --> 00:09:39.287
because Vayner had a website for quite

00:09:39.287 --> 00:09:41.350
a while that seemed, oh, I don't know,

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.583
like we were going out of business.

00:09:45.193 --> 00:09:46.685
By the way, big shout-out
to the creative team.

00:09:46.685 --> 00:09:50.145
That was all my, I don't want
anybody who builds the website

00:09:50.145 --> 00:09:51.484
for the company to get upset about that.

00:09:51.484 --> 00:09:54.216
That was all on my head, my fault.

00:09:54.216 --> 00:09:56.988
Look, I think what you do with

00:09:56.988 --> 00:09:59.130
your website needs to have a strategy.

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.524
At the time, when I was building Vayner

00:10:00.524 --> 00:10:02.717
where we had that website,
I didn't think we needed

00:10:02.717 --> 00:10:04.798
to showcase our work or our people

00:10:04.798 --> 00:10:08.068
or awards to get new
business or new talent.

00:10:08.068 --> 00:10:10.495
I wanted to be really known for what we

00:10:10.495 --> 00:10:13.241
were doing internally, it
was a very internal time,

00:10:13.241 --> 00:10:15.983
and the strategy was I didn't want

00:10:15.983 --> 00:10:18.473
anything outward messing up what I

00:10:18.473 --> 00:10:20.997
was head down doing during
that period of time.

00:10:20.997 --> 00:10:24.115
I think every website, every tweet,

00:10:24.115 --> 00:10:26.814
every Instagram photo, everything you do,

00:10:26.814 --> 00:10:29.530
the way you suck in the oxygen,

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:32.822
needs to have strategy behind it.

00:10:32.822 --> 00:10:34.106
We should really, we should expand

00:10:34.106 --> 00:10:36.918
on the strategy of the
way you consume oxygen.

00:10:36.918 --> 00:10:39.091
I'd like to see where I'd go with that.

00:10:39.091 --> 00:10:42.072
So, every action needs
to be well thought out.

00:10:42.072 --> 00:10:43.971
Do I think companies need to do that?

00:10:43.971 --> 00:10:45.992
I absolutely do not, I
think my company needed

00:10:45.992 --> 00:10:48.045
to do that because that's what I thought

00:10:48.045 --> 00:10:51.252
was the right course of action,
staying low, not making--

00:10:51.252 --> 00:10:52.904
One of the big things is that people

00:10:52.904 --> 00:10:54.227
thought I was starting an agency,

00:10:54.227 --> 00:10:57.014
that Mr. Gary Vee Crush It Twitter guy

00:10:57.014 --> 00:11:00.349
was starting an agency and
it would be a front, right?

00:11:00.349 --> 00:11:02.872
I'd sell ya on the sizzle
and then our work would suck.

00:11:02.872 --> 00:11:04.519
And that's happened so many times.

00:11:04.519 --> 00:11:08.503
I was so obsessed with
actually building a company,

00:11:09.173 --> 00:11:10.370
and so obsessed that people forgot

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.164
that I actually built a company before,

00:11:12.164 --> 00:11:14.145
that I didn't want it
to be about the sizzle

00:11:14.145 --> 00:11:16.239
or me or putting all this out stuff.

00:11:16.239 --> 00:11:19.269
So we just put our head down
and executed and the website

00:11:19.269 --> 00:11:21.991
really represented where
we were at that time.

00:11:21.991 --> 00:11:23.953
So I don't think it was tricking anyone,

00:11:23.953 --> 00:11:25.782
like, "Look over here, we stink,"

00:11:25.782 --> 00:11:27.261
and then "We're great, we got you."

00:11:27.261 --> 00:11:29.021
I think that that's a romantic way

00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:31.284
to think about it, I think the actions

